---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="What one label does to a time-series database" hint="A fleet of hosts writes one point per series every 15 seconds. Choose how points are compressed, add a label to the request counter, set the retention and block size, and watch bytes per point, series memory, disk and the cost of a dashboard query.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start with <b>user_id</b> as the extra label: the 8,000 series of 200 hosts become <b>10 million</b>, the series alone need <b>45 GB</b> (two nodes) and the fleet-wide dashboard decodes 86 billion points, about <b>5 minutes</b>. Switch the label to <b>none</b> and the same system has 8,000 series, 36 MB and answers in milliseconds. Every new label value is a new series, and series are the unit of cost.</li>
    <li>Compare the <b>compression</b> options: raw points take <b>16 bytes</b>, delta-of-delta + XOR about <b>2.1 bytes</b>, so with user_id the memory for series and head drops from 145 GB to 45 GB. The dashboard is slower with Gorilla (about 5 minutes against 2.4 minutes for raw), because decoding costs CPU: you trade processor time for memory and disk.</li>
    <li>Raise the <b>block size</b> to <b>24 hours</b> with user_id: the head must hold 1.5 blocks of points for every series, so memory rises from 45 GB to <b>214 GB</b>. At <b>1 hour</b> it falls to 38 GB, but there are more blocks, each repeating its index entries (62 GB of block indexes on disk, against 42 GB at 2 hours).</li>
    <li>Choose <b>raw for 30 days, nothing else</b>: the 30-day dashboard has no rollups to read, so it opens 360 blocks and decodes <b>1.7 trillion points</b>, hours instead of minutes. With the <b>2 years</b> rule, a <b>last year</b> dashboard still works from 1-hour rollups, while the 30-day rule shows only 30 days of the year.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg tsb" data-tsb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Compression <select class="pg-in" data-codec>
        <option value="raw">raw (8-byte time + 8-byte value)</option>
        <option value="delta">delta timestamps, raw values</option>
        <option value="gorilla" selected>delta-of-delta + XOR (Gorilla)</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Hosts <input type="range" min="10" max="1000" step="10" value="200" data-hosts /> <b data-hostsval></b></label>
      <label>Extra label on the request counter <select class="pg-in" data-label>
        <option value="none">none</option>
        <option value="endpoint">endpoint (40 values)</option>
        <option value="customer">customer_id (2,000 values)</option>
        <option value="user" selected>user_id (50,000 values)</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Retention rule <select class="pg-in" data-tiers>
        <option value="a">raw for 30 days, nothing else</option>
        <option value="b" selected>raw 7 days, 5-minute rollups 90 days</option>
        <option value="c">raw 2 days, 5-minute 30 days, 1-hour 2 years</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Block size <select class="pg-in" data-block>
        <option value="1">1 hour</option>
        <option value="2" selected>2 hours</option>
        <option value="6">6 hours</option>
        <option value="24">24 hours</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Dashboard time range <select class="pg-in" data-range>
        <option value="1">last day</option>
        <option value="30" selected>last 30 days</option>
        <option value="365">last year</option>
      </select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Bytes per point</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Series and memory</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Dashboard query</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Disk for the retention rule</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b5><h3>Without the extra label</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o5></span><span class="pg-note" data-n5></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: every host writes 40 series, and one of them is the request counter, which also carries the extra label. A host is assumed to see every value of that label. Bytes per point are measured by compressing 60 seeded series of 240 points each (steady gauges, counters and noisy gauges). A series costs 3 KB of index and bookkeeping memory, and the head holds 1.5 blocks of points. The dashboard sums the request counter for the whole fleet, using the finest tier that still covers the range. Query time is a rough estimate on 8 cores, with 25 ns to decode a Gorilla point and 0.6 microseconds to open a series in a block. A node is 64 GB, and half is usable for series.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query } from '../../playground';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-tsb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    // CORE-START
    const INTERVAL = 15; const METRICS = 40; const SAMPLE_SERIES = 60; const SAMPLE_POINTS = 240;
    const HOUR_S = 3600; const DAY_S = 86400; const HOURS_PER_DAY = 24; const BITS_PER_BYTE = 8; const MS_PER_S = 1000; const NS_PER_MS = 1e6;
    // Bit costs per point: raw is a 64-bit timestamp plus a 64-bit float; the first point of a chunk stores both in 96 bits;
    // Gorilla spends 1 bit on a repeated value, 2 + window bits when the XOR fits the previous window, and 13 + window bits (control, 5-bit lead, 6-bit length) otherwise.
    const BITS = { raw: 128, first: 96, value: 64, word: 32, smallDelta: 8, bigDelta: 16, smallDeltaMax: 128, same: 1, reuse: 2, newWindow: 13, maxLead: 31 };
    const RAW_BYTES = BITS.raw / BITS_PER_BYTE;
    const SAMPLE = { seed: 11, kinds: [0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 2], counterStart: 1000, gaugeBase: 40, startT: 1700000000, step: 0.25, counterMaxStep: 4, noiseBase: 30, noiseRange: 100000, noiseScale: 1000, lateOneIn: 8 }; // seeded sample series: 0 steady gauge, 1 counter, 2 noisy gauge
    const HEAD_BLOCKS = 1.5; // blocks of recent points kept in memory
    const BLOCK_INDEX_B = 24; // bytes per series per block for the block's own index
    const ROLLUP_FIELDS = 4; // a rollup point stores four aggregates
    const QUERY = { openMsPerSeriesBlock: 0.0006, diskBps: 2e9, parallel: 8 }; // cost to open a block per series, disk read rate, query threads
    const FIVE_MIN_S = 300;
    const BUDGET_MS = 10000; // dashboard latency budget
    const BLOWUP = 10; // series multiplier that counts as a cardinality explosion
    const DISK_WARN_B = 20e12; // disk use that turns the card red
    const dv = new DataView(new ArrayBuffer(8));
    const ctz32 = (x: number) => 31 - Math.clz32(x & -x);
    // Gorilla delta-of-delta buckets: 1, 9, 12, 16 or 36 bits.
    const dodBits = (d: number) => (d === 0 ? 1 : d >= -63 && d <= 64 ? 9 : d >= -255 && d <= 256 ? 12 : d >= -2047 && d <= 2048 ? 16 : 36);
    // Count the bits each encoding needs for the same seeded points (no bits are written, only counted).
    function sampleCosts() {
      let seed = SAMPLE.seed; const rnd = (n: number) => { // Numerical Recipes LCG
        seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296; return Math.floor(seed / 65536) % n; };
      let rawBits = 0; let deltaBits = 0; let gorBits = 0; let points = 0;
      for (let s = 0; s < SAMPLE_SERIES; s++) {
        const kind = SAMPLE.kinds[s % SAMPLE.kinds.length]; let v = kind === 1 ? SAMPLE.counterStart : SAMPLE.gaugeBase + s; let t = SAMPLE.startT; let prevDelta = 0;
        let prevHi = 0; let prevLo = 0; let lead = -1; let len = 0;
        for (let i = 0; i < SAMPLE_POINTS; i++) {
          if (kind === 0) { if (rnd(2) === 0) v += (rnd(3) - 1) * SAMPLE.step; } // steady gauge: moves in quarter steps half the time
          else if (kind === 1) v += rnd(SAMPLE.counterMaxStep); // counter: grows by small whole numbers
          else v = SAMPLE.noiseBase + rnd(SAMPLE.noiseRange) / SAMPLE.noiseScale; // noisy gauge: arbitrary decimals at every scrape
          const nt = i === 0 ? t : t + INTERVAL + (rnd(SAMPLE.lateOneIn) === 0 ? 1 : 0);
          const delta = nt - t; const dod = delta - prevDelta; t = nt; prevDelta = delta;
          dv.setFloat64(0, v); const hi = dv.getUint32(0); const lo = dv.getUint32(4);
          points++; rawBits += BITS.raw;
          if (i === 0) { deltaBits += BITS.first; gorBits += BITS.first; prevHi = hi; prevLo = lo; continue; }
          deltaBits += (delta < BITS.smallDeltaMax ? BITS.smallDelta : BITS.bigDelta) + BITS.value; gorBits += dodBits(dod);
          const xh = (hi ^ prevHi) >>> 0; const xl = (lo ^ prevLo) >>> 0; prevHi = hi; prevLo = lo;
          if (xh === 0 && xl === 0) { gorBits += BITS.same; continue; } // same value as before: one bit
          const l = Math.min(xh ? Math.clz32(xh) : BITS.word + Math.clz32(xl), BITS.maxLead); const tz = xl ? ctz32(xl) : BITS.word + ctz32(xh);
          if (lead >= 0 && l >= lead && tz >= BITS.value - lead - len) gorBits += BITS.reuse + len; // fits the previous window of meaningful bits
          else { const m = BITS.value - l - tz; gorBits += BITS.newWindow + m; lead = l; len = m; }
        }
      }
      return { raw: rawBits / points / BITS_PER_BYTE, delta: deltaBits / points / BITS_PER_BYTE, gorilla: gorBits / points / BITS_PER_BYTE } as Record<string, number>;
    }
    const DECODE_NS: Record<string, number> = { raw: 3, delta: 8, gorilla: 25 };
    const LABELS: Record<string, { name: string; values: number }> = { none: { name: 'no extra label', values: 1 }, endpoint: { name: 'endpoint', values: 40 }, customer: { name: 'customer_id', values: 2000 }, user: { name: 'user_id', values: 50000 } };
    const TIERS: Record<string, { res: number; days: number }[]> = {
      a: [{ res: 15, days: 30 }],
      b: [{ res: 15, days: 7 }, { res: 300, days: 90 }],
      c: [{ res: 15, days: 2 }, { res: 300, days: 30 }, { res: 3600, days: 730 }],
    };
    const ROLLUP_BLOCK_H: Record<number, number> = { 300: 24, 3600: 168 }; // rollup blocks are always longer than raw blocks
    const INDEX_B = 3000;
    type Cfg = { codec: string; hosts: number; label: string; tiers: string; blockH: number; rangeDays: number };
    function model(cfg: Cfg, cost: Record<string, number>) {
      const bpp = cost[cfg.codec]; const d = LABELS[cfg.label].values;
      const reqSeries = cfg.hosts * d; const series = cfg.hosts * (METRICS - 1) + reqSeries;
      const headPts = HEAD_BLOCKS * (HOUR_S / INTERVAL) * cfg.blockH; // 1.5 blocks of points at one point per 15 s
      const indexMem = series * INDEX_B; const headMem = series * headPts * bpp; const mem = indexMem + headMem;
      const tiers = TIERS[cfg.tiers]; let disk = 0; let blockIdx = 0;
      tiers.forEach((t) => {
        const bh = t.res === INTERVAL ? cfg.blockH : ROLLUP_BLOCK_H[t.res];
        blockIdx += Math.ceil((t.days * HOURS_PER_DAY) / bh) * series * BLOCK_INDEX_B; // each block repeats its own index entries, about 24 bytes per series
        disk += series * (DAY_S / t.res) * t.days * bpp * (t.res === INTERVAL ? 1 : ROLLUP_FIELDS);
      });
      const tier = tiers.find((t) => t.days >= cfg.rangeDays); const used = tier ?? tiers[tiers.length - 1];
      const availDays = Math.min(cfg.rangeDays, used.days);
      const bh = used.res === INTERVAL ? cfg.blockH : ROLLUP_BLOCK_H[used.res];
      const blocks = used.res === INTERVAL ? Math.ceil(Math.max(0, availDays * HOURS_PER_DAY - HEAD_BLOCKS * cfg.blockH) / bh) + 1 : Math.ceil((availDays * HOURS_PER_DAY) / bh); // +1 is the in-memory head
      const points = (reqSeries * availDays * DAY_S) / used.res; const bytesRead = points * bpp;
      const ms = (blocks * reqSeries * QUERY.openMsPerSeriesBlock + (points * DECODE_NS[cfg.codec]) / NS_PER_MS + (bytesRead / QUERY.diskBps) * MS_PER_S) / QUERY.parallel;
      return { bpp, d, reqSeries, series, indexMem, headMem, mem, disk, blockIdx, used, covered: !!tier, availDays, blocks, points, ms };
    }
    // CORE-END
    const cost = sampleCosts();
    const NODE = 32e9; // usable memory per node
    const fmtN = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
    const fmtB = (b: number) => (b >= 1e12 ? `${(b / 1e12).toFixed(1)} TB` : b >= 1e9 ? `${(b / 1e9).toFixed(1)} GB` : b >= 1e6 ? `${(b / 1e6).toFixed(0)} MB` : `${(b / 1e3).toFixed(0)} KB`);
    const fmtT = (ms: number) => (ms < 1000 ? `${Math.max(1, Math.round(ms))} ms` : ms < 60000 ? `${(ms / 1000).toFixed(1)} s` : ms < 3.6e6 ? `${Math.round(ms / 60000)} min` : ms < 8.64e7 ? `${Math.round(ms / 3.6e6)} hours` : `${Math.round(ms / 8.64e7)} days`);
    const fmtP = (p: number) => (p >= 1e9 ? `${(p / 1e9).toFixed(1)} billion` : p >= 1e6 ? `${(p / 1e6).toFixed(1)} million` : fmtN(p));
    const tierName = (res: number) => (res === INTERVAL ? `raw ${INTERVAL} s points` : res === FIVE_MIN_S ? '5-minute rollups' : '1-hour rollups');
    function draw() {
      const cfg: Cfg = { codec: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-codec]').value, hosts: Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-hosts]').value), label: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-label]').value, tiers: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-tiers]').value, blockH: Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-block]').value), rangeDays: Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-range]').value) };
      q('[data-hostsval]').textContent = String(cfg.hosts);
      const m = model(cfg, cost); const base = model({ ...cfg, label: 'none' }, cost);
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `${m.bpp.toFixed(1)} bytes`; q('[data-n1]').textContent = `${(RAW_BYTES / m.bpp).toFixed(1)} times smaller than raw (${RAW_BYTES} bytes). Measured on ${SAMPLE_SERIES * SAMPLE_POINTS} seeded points.`;
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = `${fmtN(m.series)} series, ${fmtB(m.mem)}`;
      const nodes = Math.ceil(m.mem / NODE);
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = `index ${fmtB(m.indexMem)} plus head points ${fmtB(m.headMem)}. ${nodes === 1 ? 'Fits on one node.' : `Needs ${nodes} nodes just to hold the series.`}`;
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = `${fmtN(m.reqSeries)} series, ${fmtT(m.ms)}`;
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = `${m.blocks} blocks opened, ${fmtP(m.points)} points decoded from ${tierName(m.used.res)}${m.covered ? '' : `. Only ${m.availDays} of ${cfg.rangeDays} days exist`}.`;
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = fmtB(m.disk); q('[data-n4]').textContent = `of which block indexes ${fmtB(m.blockIdx)}. One copy.`;
      q('[data-o5]').textContent = `${fmtN(base.series)} series, ${fmtB(base.mem)}`; q('[data-n5]').textContent = `${base.reqSeries === m.reqSeries ? 'This is the same system.' : `The label multiplies the request counter by ${fmtN(m.d)}: ${fmtN(m.series / base.series)} times the series and ${fmtN(m.mem / base.mem)} times the memory.`}`;
      const slow = m.ms > BUDGET_MS; const tooBig = nodes > 1; const blow = m.series / base.series >= BLOWUP;
      const color = (el: string, bad: boolean) => q<HTMLElement>(el).style.setProperty('--c', bad ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      color('[data-b1]', false); color('[data-b2]', tooBig); color('[data-b3]', slow || !m.covered); color('[data-b4]', m.disk > DISK_WARN_B); color('[data-b5]', false);
      const parts: string[] = [];
      if (blow) parts.push(`${LABELS[cfg.label].name} gives the request counter ${fmtN(m.d)} values on each of ${cfg.hosts} hosts, so ${fmtN(base.series)} series become ${fmtN(m.series)}. Every one needs its index entry and head chunk whether or not it is ever queried.`);
      if (tooBig) parts.push(`The series alone need ${fmtB(m.mem)} of memory, more than one node can use.`);
      if (slow) parts.push(`The dashboard decodes ${fmtP(m.points)} points and would take about ${fmtT(m.ms)}, past a ${BUDGET_MS / MS_PER_S} second budget. Rollups only coarsen time and keep every series, so fewer series is the real fix.`);
      if (!m.covered) parts.push(`The retention rule keeps only ${m.used.days} days, so a ${cfg.rangeDays}-day dashboard shows a truncated graph.`);
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); const bad = parts.length > 0; out.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      out.textContent = bad ? parts.join(' ') : `Healthy: ${fmtN(m.series)} series fit in ${fmtB(m.mem)}, and the dashboard reads ${fmtP(m.points)} points from ${tierName(m.used.res)} in about ${fmtT(m.ms)}.`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw); root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
